 r←Test_GETRefreshStatus_Fields url;Assert;Authed;IsDT;NullOrDT;d;dt;res
⍝ Check GET /admin/refresh/status returns the documented fields with correct types
 r←0
 Assert←##.Assert
 Authed←##.MAIN.Authed
 dt←1 1 1 1 2 1 1 2 1 1 3 1 1 4 1 1 4 1 1         ⍝ DateTime type signature, as Test_GETProfiling_Response
 IsDT←{dt≡1 2 3 4+.×⍨⍵∘.∊⎕D'-' 'T' ':'}
 NullOrDT←{((⊂'null')≡⍵)∨IsDT ⍵}                  ⍝ Timestamps are an ISO string until first set, then null
 
 res←('GET'Authed url,'/admin/refresh/status').Run
 'Expected 200 OK'Assert 200=res.HttpStatus
 d←res.Data
 'status must be idle or running'Assert(⊂d.status)∊'idle' 'running'
 'pending must be 0 or 1'Assert d.pending∊0 1
 'started_at must be null or a datetime'Assert NullOrDT d.started_at
 'finished_at must be null or a datetime'Assert NullOrDT d.finished_at
 'last_success_at must be null or a datetime'Assert NullOrDT d.last_success_at
 'last_error_at must be null or a datetime'Assert NullOrDT d.last_error_at
 'last_error_message must be a character vector'Assert 1≥≡d.last_error_message
⍝ running and thread are the lock itself, not part of the API
 'running must not be exposed'Assert 0=d.⎕NC'running'
 'thread must not be exposed'Assert 0=d.⎕NC'thread'
 r←1
